---
description: Architectural invariants for orchestration, harnesses, Git lifecycle, permissions, and state
alwaysApply: true
---
- The orchestration engine is harness-neutral.
- Harness adapters own model/binary/protocol details.
- Executor performs implementation and quality commands; reviewer makes decisions from evidence.
- One run equals one AI branch; one approved stage equals one stage-named commit.
- Never automatically push or merge.
- Permission and plan-review budgets must not become accidental stage blockers.
- UI consumes semantic events and never controls business state.
